From: Remy <remy@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64: clear the download-mode cookie during boot, not only at reset

REVIEW-20261031-2230 F-5: the download-mode cookie was cleared
only in kreset()/emergency_reset(). A reset that bypasses
kreset - the P3 watchdog bite at +45 s on 2026-10-31 - finds
the cookie still set and lands in Qualcomm CrashDump Mode.
With the qcom-dload-mode-clear feature, qcom_scm::init() now
also clears the cookie as soon as SCM availability is known
(the earliest sound call site: PSCI firmware calls already
execute in this phase, logging is live, the attempt is the
bounded <=16-retry query and can never block boot). Success
prints the 0038 line at boot; failure is a warning. The
kreset/emergency clears stay.

Agent: Remy (root of record)
Model: Muse Wonder (muse-wonder-1.0)
Provider: Meta

---
diff --git a/src/arch/aarch64/device/qcom_scm.rs b/src/arch/aarch64/device/qcom_scm.rs
index 7d2486a1..356888ce 100644
--- a/src/arch/aarch64/device/qcom_scm.rs
+++ b/src/arch/aarch64/device/qcom_scm.rs
@@ -1,7 +1,12 @@
 //! Narrow Qualcomm SCM support for clearing the download-mode cookie.
 //!
 //! This is opt-in because the OnePlus 6 firmware call has not been verified on
-//! hardware. The normal reset path never invokes these SMC calls.
+//! hardware. Builds without the `qcom-dload-mode-clear` feature never invoke
+//! these SMC calls. With the feature, the cookie is cleared during boot
+//! (from init(), patch 0042) as well as in the reset entrypoints, so a
+//! reset that bypasses kreset() - a watchdog bite, a panic, a power cut -
+//! still lands in the normal boot path instead of Qualcomm CrashDump
+//! Mode (REVIEW-20261031-2230 F-5).
 
 use core::arch::asm;
 use core::sync::atomic::{AtomicBool, Ordering};
@@ -34,6 +39,26 @@ pub fn init(fdt: &Fdt<'_>) {
     if present {
         info!("Qualcomm SCM node found; download-mode clear remains opt-in");
     }
+    // P3 F-5 (REVIEW-20261031-2230): with the opt-in feature, also clear
+    // the download-mode cookie here, during boot - not only in the
+    // reset entrypoints. A reset that bypasses kreset() (a watchdog
+    // bite, a panic, a power cut) otherwise finds the cookie still set
+    // and lands in Qualcomm CrashDump Mode. This is the earliest sound
+    // call site: init() is the first moment SCM availability is known,
+    // PSCI firmware calls already execute in this phase (psci::init ran
+    // immediately before), and logging is live. The attempt is bounded
+    // (the availability query retries at most 16 times) and a failure
+    // is only a warning - it never blocks boot, and the
+    // kreset()/emergency_reset() clears stay in place regardless. The
+    // result line is the same one patch 0038 added to the reset paths,
+    // so the boot-time clear is visible on the panel/serial as well.
+    #[cfg(feature = "qcom-dload-mode-clear")]
+    if present {
+        match clear_download_mode() {
+            Ok(()) => { info!("qcom SCM: download-mode cleared"); }
+            Err(reason) => { warn!("Qualcomm SCM download-mode clear failed: {}", reason); }
+        }
+    }
 }
 
 /// Clears Qualcomm's download-mode cookie when the opt-in feature is enabled.
